                <pb facs="0169" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">345.1121 Benz, Heinrich/8: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Calcutta</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Groth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-09-18T19:00:00-04:00">September 18,
                            1940—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s July 27, 4 p.m. Telegraph briefly reply of Indian Government in
                    regard to the Benz case. If a reply has not yet been received you should request
                    that it be expedited.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
